            "review_text": "mebrendel\nHamburg, Germany2 contributions\n0\nBest Indian restaurant in Mui Ne\nDec 2024 • Couples\nMy wife and me have been there three times so far and will go again tomorrow. The owner and Chef is from North India so we went for the North Indian dishes. (Ganesh offers also South Indian food that we did not try so far.) Masala Papadam comes with the Masala aside, so you can add the Masala table spoon wise before eating and the papadam does not get soaked. Very good idea. Chef´s special is a chicken curry called Ganesh made according to his mother's recipe and it also tastes likewise: we can imagine the Chef as a kid sitting in the kitchen and waiting for his mum to come up with it. Delicious. Everything is homemade and therefore unique in taste, even the mango chutney. We came here first in 2001 and ever since. Our last visit was in 2010. Now again. Top place in Mui Ne whereas you will not find it when looking for Restaurants in Mui Ne. One has to type in Phan Thiet instead. That's a bit sad and may explain why mostly insiders eat here.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 11, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-03",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
